        {
          "type": "text",
          "plain_text": " by Charlotte and Peter Fiell (Taschen) is as close to a single-volume survey of the field as you'll find. The current edition runs to 512 pages with in-depth entries on 125 designers and design-led companies, and it's arranged by what things are made of rather than by country: furniture, glass, ceramics, textiles, jewellery, metalware and product design, 1900 to the present day. Reach for it first and the other four make more sense. ",
          "href": null,
