            "strikethrough": false,
            "underline": false
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "plain_text": " is Denmark, Norway and Sweden, so Scandinavian design tends to mean the furniture, the mid-century Danish and Swedish chairs and cabinets above all. Nordic is the bigger tent, Finland and Iceland included, and it's the word you need for Alvar Aalto, for Iittala glass and for Marimekko, all Finnish. Fiell's book covers the Finns properly and still calls itself Scandinavian, which tells you how loosely both words get used once you're standing in a bookshop.",
          "href": null,
          "text": {
            "content": " is Denmark, Norway and Sweden, so Scandinavian design tends to mean the furniture, the mid-century Danish and Swedish chairs and cabinets above all. Nordic is the bigger tent, Finland and Iceland included, and it's the word you need for Alvar Aalto, for Iittala glass and for Marimekko, all Finnish. Fiell's book covers the Finns properly and still calls itself Scandinavian, which tells you how loosely both words get used once you're standing in a bookshop.",
            "link": null
          },
          "annotations": {
            "bold": false,
